{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "feature": "catalog-expansion",
  "scope": "User-accepted roughly ninefold expansion from the 905-model, six-kit baseline across all asset categories, with distinct source-model accounting, licensed provenance, Castle decode and geometry validation, coherent scale/materials, context-aware playable WFC placement, searchable desktop/phone selection, and bounded optional loading that preserves startup and ongoing world performance.",
  "criticAgent": "Luna",
  "builderAgent": "/root",
  "decision": "changes_requested",
  "grades": {
    "intuitiveness": {
      "grade": "B",
      "evidence": "The final object browser journey passes 188 checks across desktop and phone alternatives, with category, subgroup and name/group search, explicit no-match feedback, 44-pixel filter targets, breadcrumbs, object selection, Undo/Redo and recovery. The interaction is clear for the admitted 14 interior objects and retained regional choices. Most of the 8,365-model library still has no player-facing search or contextual selection path, so full catalog intuitiveness is not demonstrated."
    },
    "accuracy": {
      "grade": "C",
      "evidence": "The acquisition and static validation evidence is substantial: the catalog records 8,365 distinct GLB/glTF outputs with source and license accounting, and the object batch binds 32 optional profiles to manifests, source hashes, Castle geometry, POSITION counts, bounds and PNG dimensions. The final 14-object browser journey and 4,609 native world checks verify real rendering, WFC mutation, leases, exact unrelated-node preservation, Undo/Redo and graphics recovery for that subset. Full-scope category admission, context-aware placement, animation/collision/support validation and ongoing-world performance for the accepted library remain unverified."
    },
    "wowFactor": {
      "grade": "B",
      "evidence": "The inspected object and recovery captures show varied books, artifacts, equipment and food rendered at useful close range, with coherent Phanes controls and readable phone browsing. The final evidence improves the renamed Stoppered vial presentation and adds the Croissant and other object profiles. The broad library still lacks representative playable captures across terrain, structures, vehicles, people, animals, industrial assets and effects, so visual coherence and demonstration quality for the full expansion cannot receive B+."
    },
    "thinkingOutOfTheBox": {
      "grade": "B+",
      "evidence": "The delta uses a practical separation between immutable source admission, interior-domain role metadata, measured conservative envelopes, content-aware WFC support and lazy Castle resource leases. Search filters remain non-mutating until an actual object choice, and the existing world transaction supplies exact preservation and recovery. This is a useful pattern for growing a catalog, though it does not by itself solve the remaining full-catalog placement and performance work."
    }
  },
  "blockingFindings": [
    "The full catalog-expansion gate remains open: only 12 new interior objects plus two earlier interior leaves and 18 regional profiles are admitted to player-facing WFC/application paths. Extend measured category-specific admission and playable placement across the required terrain, structures, modular construction/routes, furniture, industrial equipment, vehicles, people/animals and surfaces/effects, with explicit scale, collision, support, animation and role constraints where applicable.",
    "Provide a reproducible end-to-end performance and lifetime qualification for representative populated worlds using the optional library: startup remains bounded, on-demand loading/cancellation and retirement remain safe during ongoing authoring, and desktop/phone rendering stays usable. The current source totals and distinct-profile counters are not GPU-memory, instance-count or FPS evidence.",
    "Complete broad desktop/phone catalog journeys that demonstrate searchable choices, coherent materials and contextual WFC placement beyond the 14-object interior subset. Preserve the current 188-check subset evidence and its exact source/license provenance while expanding coverage."
  ],
  "resolvedFindings": [
    "The twelve-object delta is registered with immutable IDs, source and manifest hashes, category/subgroup/role metadata, conservative physical dimensions and measured triangles, vertices and texture pixels. The renamed display label is consistent with the unchanged potion source identity.",
    "The final object browser journey passes 188 checks, including all 14 interior admissions, alternate desktop/phone controls, breadcrumb and child selection, category/subgroup/search/no-match behavior, real Castle rendering and lease ownership, exact unrelated composition and regional mask preservation, Undo/Redo and actual graphics recovery.",
    "The native object verifier passes 1,018 profile/source/manifest/geometry checks, while the extended world/interior run passes 4,609 assertions for all fourteen interior profiles. The release build passes in build/logs/catalog-objects-main-build-02.log, with final browser errors and shader-failure diagnostics empty."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is an independent retained-evidence review of the full registered scope; no browser, GPU or native suite was rerun because the candidate and provenance were frozen and the targeted final runs were available.",
    "The 8,365-model inspector establishes static decode, finite transformed bounds and rendered triangles. It does not establish animation playback, collision, doors, support surfaces, WFC eligibility, contextual placement or coherent visual treatment.",
    "The combined optional counters describe 32 distinct admitted profiles and conservative staged/source costs. They do not measure every placed instance, decoded total, browser-internal buffers, GPU allocation, thermal behavior or phone FPS.",
    "The object browser's 29 retained PNGs and 188 checks cover the 14 interior profiles and recovery subset; they do not constitute all-category catalog coverage or full release acceptance. The registry's full catalog-expansion feature remains held."
  ],
  "verification": "Independent Luna review inspected src/phanes.catalog.objects.pas and admission delegation, current interior catalog/UI and filter markup, object/house/native/browser test inputs, catalog object documentation, full expansion requirements and retained bounded runtime/publication/regional evidence. build/catalog-objects-02 records 1,018 native admission checks and build/logs/catalog-objects-world-test-03.log records 4,609 world/profile checks. build/catalog-objects-browser-02/result.txt records 188 PASS checks with final empty error and shader-failure diagnostics and 29 retained PNGs; build/catalog-objects-browser-02/provenance.json and build/catalog-objects-provenance-02.json bind current sources and artifacts. The accepted inventory remains 8,365 models from 108 kits, while player-facing admission is only the tested subset. The current registry contains 98 unique existing inputs; reviewedFiles contains exactly those declared inputs and evidenceFingerprints separately retains cited build, provenance and capture artifacts. No browser, GPU or native suite was rerun by this critic.",
